+View the Config
+---------------
+
+To inspect the configuration of your application, you can use the
+:func:`config <cli.config_command>` command. This prints the entire
+configuration as JSON. Sensitive values are masked: any key containing
+``SECRET``, ``PASSWORD``, ``TOKEN``, or ``KEY`` (case-insensitive) will
+have its value displayed as ``"***"``. ::
+
+    $ flask config
+    {
+      "DEBUG": false,
+      "SECRET_KEY": "***",
+      "DATABASE_URL": "postgresql://localhost/mydb",
+      "API_TOKEN": "***"
+    }
+
+
